Pydantic Input Validation Engine
A lightweight Python module designed to ingest, validate, and sanitize incoming raw JSON payloads (such as customer reviews) against strict schema rules before any downstream processing or LLM execution occurs.

Features
Strict Pattern Matching: Enforces regular expressions on fields like review IDs (^R\d{5}$) and star rating formats.

Automatic Type Coercion & Parsing: Seamlessly converts ISO date strings (e.g., 2025-01-01) into native Python datetime.date objects during validation.

Length Constraints: Protects downstream token budgets and systems by enforcing strict character bounds (min_length and max_length).

Immediate Fail-Fast Validation: Rejects malformed or malicious payloads instantly, preventing wasted LLM API costs and guarding against pipeline corruption.

